00:53:16.770 --> 00:53:18.730
have actually gotten to a fight on camera.

1271
00:53:18.770 --> 00:53:19.830
So it was like a big deal.

1272
00:53:19.830 --> 00:53:23.690
And the writers were extremely particular about how the fight should sound.

1273
00:53:23.830 --> 00:53:27.150
So they ended up like rewriting it on the spot several different times.

1274
00:53:27.330 --> 00:53:30.950
We did several different versions, which meant I had to keep singing that song,

1275
00:53:31.010 --> 00:53:35.630
which wasn't great for my voice, and probably became progressively worse and worse as we went.

1276
00:53:35.950 --> 00:53:39.630
But for the very last take, I remember we had done it so many times.

1277
00:53:39.630 --> 00:53:40.630
And I was just like, you know what?

1278
00:53:40.770 --> 00:53:41.250
Screw it.

1279
00:53:41.670 --> 00:53:45.210
And I was singing to you, and you were arguing with Jim while I was singing.

1280
00:53:45.210 --> 00:53:49.390
So I took my finger, my index finger, and put it towards your mouth to shush you.

1281
00:53:49.870 --> 00:53:50.910
And you broke.

1282
00:53:51.070 --> 00:53:51.750
You laughed.

1283
00:53:51.990 --> 00:53:53.670
But it was so funny.

1284
00:53:53.770 --> 00:53:54.410
We were all laughing.

1285
00:53:54.410 --> 00:53:55.650
I'll never forget that moment.

1286
00:53:55.810 --> 00:53:57.490
It was the best of my life.

1287
00:53:57.810 --> 00:54:00.110
And you said that was so brilliant.

1288
00:54:00.210 --> 00:54:02.270
And luckily, it made the cut.

1289
00:54:02.430 --> 00:54:06.070
You see in the video me raising my finger to shush you.

1290
00:54:06.290 --> 00:54:07.410
But yeah, that was so fun.

1291
00:54:07.410 --> 00:54:08.710
And that's something I'll never forget.

1292
00:54:09.950 --> 00:54:11.910
So, lady, I remember when he did that.

1293
00:54:12.110 --> 00:54:15.310
I remember when he put his finger up to my face to shush me.

1294
00:54:15.510 --> 00:54:19.270
I can't believe we had enough footage to keep it in the episode,

1295
00:54:19.270 --> 00:54:23.610
because I felt like I immediately broke, because I thought that was so funny.

1296
00:54:23.990 --> 00:54:29.770
But the whole thing was like, he was so earnestly, sweetly singing right in my face.

1297
00:54:29.950 --> 00:54:30.090
Yeah.

1298
00:54:30.330 --> 00:54:32.650
It was hard to keep a straight face the whole time.

1299
00:54:33.090 --> 00:54:35.250
You know, after we filmed this conference room scene,

1300
00:54:35.250 --> 00:54:39.450
Nick shared that he had a very interesting encounter with Rainn Wilson.

1301
00:54:39.670 --> 00:54:39.970
Yeah.

1302
00:54:40.270 --> 00:54:41.930
He sent in an audio clip about it.

1303
00:54:42.050 --> 00:54:47.110
I want you to hear it, because Rainn was not the curmudgeon we know him to be.

1304
00:54:47.310 --> 00:54:49.730
He was the other part of Rainn.

1305
00:54:49.890 --> 00:54:51.870
He was, and he changed Nick's life.

1306
00:54:51.870 --> 00:54:52.310
He did.

1307
00:54:52.470 --> 00:54:53.170
Here's the clip.

1308
00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:59.490
Another moment I'll never forget, and actually had a huge impact on my life and my life trajectory,

1309
00:55:01.410 --> 00:55:06.470
was after the conference room scene, or during the conference room scene, in between takes,

1310
00:55:06.930 --> 00:55:11.410
Rainn Wilson was sitting right next to where me and my a cappella group were standing,

1311
00:55:11.410 --> 00:55:15.570
and he started a conversation, and he said, hey, so are you guys actors?

1312
00:55:16.150 --> 00:55:19.490
And we were like, no, we're from University of Virginia.

1313
00:55:19.490 --> 00:55:22.170
We're just here, you know, to play the a cappella group.

1314
00:55:22.310 --> 00:55:23.510
We're a cappella group singers.

1315
00:55:24.110 --> 00:55:26.950
And he pointed to me, and he said, you should be an actor.

1316
00:55:27.170 --> 00:55:29.590
You should consider doing this.

1317
00:55:30.410 --> 00:55:34.010
And this was after I had a scene with a few lines and sang.

1318
00:55:34.250 --> 00:55:40.910
And I was like so starstruck and taken aback by that, but it really meant a lot to me,

1319
00:55:40.910 --> 00:55:49.150
and truly is one of the reasons I decided to move out to Los Angeles after I graduated

1320
00:55:49.150 --> 00:55:51.270
and to pursue this career.

1321
00:55:51.270 --> 00:55:57.170
So thank you to Rainn Wilson for saying that to me and for giving me a vote of confidence,

1322
00:55:57.170 --> 00:56:02.470
and you've really had a big impact on my life, and I hope that I get to meet him again one day

1323
00:56:02.470 --> 00:56:05.330
so I can thank him in person, because it really meant a lot to me.

1324
00:56:06.270 --> 00:56:07.310
So there you go.

1325
00:56:07.490 --> 00:56:11.010
Nick had his Molly Shannon moment with Rainn.

1326
00:56:11.090 --> 00:56:11.770
Oh, yes.

1327
00:56:11.870 --> 00:56:14.910
This is your Molly Shannon moment where she told you to stick with it.

1328
00:56:15.030 --> 00:56:15.270
Yes.

1329
00:56:15.410 --> 00:56:17.310
I met her right when I first got to L.A.

1330
00:56:17.310 --> 00:56:20.310
And so Nick took Rainn's advice.

1331
00:56:20.370 --> 00:56:21.710
He moved to L.A.

1332
00:56:22.090 --> 00:56:23.610
He's been in a bunch of commercials.

1333
00:56:23.610 --> 00:56:28.390
He's been on Blackish and 9-1-1, and he is currently in the Sunday company at Groundlings.

1334
00:56:28.710 --> 00:56:32.990
He's also teamed up with Halstead again and Claire again on different projects.

1335
00:56:32.990 --> 00:56:34.530
He's now a working actor.

1336
00:56:34.530 --> 00:56:35.650
This is so crazy.

1337
00:56:35.650 --> 00:56:41.090
All from this, like, random email that he got one day he was in college.

1338
00:56:41.470 --> 00:56:48.710
You know, Nick's in one last clip for us, you guys, and it's about, well, it's about things you learn on set.

1339
00:56:48.990 --> 00:56:58.650
And one of the guys in the a cappella group learned that, well, he didn't understand how the toilet worked in the trailer that they were using.

1340
00:57:00.370 --> 00:57:02.410
And I think for anyone coming to L.A.

1341
00:57:02.470 --> 00:57:06.090
who wants to be an actor, this is an important lesson to learn.

1342
00:57:06.270 --> 00:57:06.770
Let's hear it.

1343
00:57:07.310 --> 00:57:07.710
Okay.

1344
00:57:07.810 --> 00:57:14.390
So this story is one that you would probably never share, but I have to tell you because it's just too outrageous to not.

1345
00:57:15.410 --> 00:57:17.110
When we were there, there were eight of us.

1346
00:57:17.210 --> 00:57:22.470
And so we all got trailers on set, and we shared them with each other, these little honey wagons.

1347
00:57:22.770 --> 00:57:24.670
There were two per each trailer.

1348
00:57:24.670 --> 00:57:26.150
And the trailers are small.

1349
00:57:26.290 --> 00:57:31.530
They have, like, a little couch and, you know, a little closet to put your costumes in and a tiny little bathroom.

1350
00:57:32.330 --> 00:57:42.270
And I remember I shared my trailer with one of my fellow a cappella group members whose name I will not mention for reasons that will soon become obvious.

1351
00:57:42.590 --> 00:57:44.450
And I remember he was in the trailer.

1352
00:57:44.450 --> 00:57:46.510
I was going to go get fitted.

1353
00:57:46.630 --> 00:57:50.230
When my fitting was done, I came back to walk up the stairs to our trailer.

1354
00:57:50.230 --> 00:57:59.070
And as I did, he burst through the door carrying a giant wad of paper towels and kind of, like, rushing down the stairs past me.

1355
00:57:59.570 --> 00:58:01.130
And I was like, okay, that's strange.

1356
00:58:01.130 --> 00:58:03.410
And he went and threw them in a trash can.

1357
00:58:03.510 --> 00:58:04.850
I was like, okay, cool.

1358
00:58:05.010 --> 00:58:05.910
That was a lot of paper towels.

1359
00:58:06.110 --> 00:58:07.190
I get back in the trailer.

1360
00:58:07.350 --> 00:58:07.950
I'm sitting there.

1361
00:58:08.070 --> 00:58:08.750
He comes in.

1362
00:58:09.090 --> 00:58:11.570
And I'm like, oh, it smells off in here.

1363
00:58:12.330 --> 00:58:16.110
Did you, like, you know, pass gas or use the bathroom?

1364
00:58:16.210 --> 00:58:17.210
And he was like, no, no, no, no.

1365
00:58:17.210 --> 00:58:18.670
And I was like, dude, are you sure?

1366
00:58:18.790 --> 00:58:22.930
Like, it smells like somebody went to the bathroom and took a poop.

1367
00:58:23.050 --> 00:58:23.910
And I was like, are you sure?

1368
00:58:24.070 --> 00:58:25.870
He's like, okay, yes, I did.

1369
00:58:26.070 --> 00:58:28.210
I used, went to the bathroom and the toilet.

1370
00:58:28.430 --> 00:58:30.050
And I, it doesn't work.

1371
00:58:30.130 --> 00:58:30.870
It doesn't flush.

1372
00:58:31.250 --> 00:58:36.530
So I had to take all the paper towels and pick it up and throw it out in the trash.

1373
00:58:36.970 --> 00:58:39.250
And I was like, oh, my God.

1374
00:58:39.670 --> 00:58:40.910
Are you kidding me?

1375
00:58:41.210 --> 00:58:45.210
It turned out the toilet was one of the ones that had a foot pedal.

1376
00:58:45.210 --> 00:58:49.310
There's a pedal underneath the toilet that you push down with your foot and it flushes.

1377
00:58:49.430 --> 00:58:51.410
And he didn't know that and couldn't find it.

1378
00:58:51.510 --> 00:58:53.390
He just thought it was a broken toilet.

1379
00:58:53.590 --> 00:59:00.050
So he panicked, wrapped his hands in paper towels, and picked up his own mess, ran it

1380
00:59:00.050 --> 00:59:03.850
through the door, and threw it away in a trash can.

1381
00:59:05.310 --> 00:59:08.030
I was mortified to hear this.

1382
00:59:08.110 --> 00:59:11.210
I have never heard of more unhinged behavior.

1383
00:59:11.750 --> 00:59:14.110
I was like, dude, it's just a foot pedal.

1384
00:59:14.110 --> 00:59:16.450
You have ruined Dunder Mifflin.

1385
00:59:16.830 --> 00:59:24.670
This is, so, yeah, to anybody who emptied the trash over there, I apologize on his behalf.

1386
00:59:25.490 --> 00:59:26.870
Yeah, I know that's disgusting.

1387
00:59:26.890 --> 00:59:28.950
But I mean, it's just so outrageous.

1388
00:59:28.950 --> 00:59:29.970
You can't make that stuff up.

1389
00:59:30.070 --> 00:59:30.650
I had to share it.

1390
00:59:30.790 --> 00:59:31.030
Sorry.

1391
00:59:32.730 --> 00:59:35.050
Here's my question after hearing that story.

1392
00:59:35.610 --> 00:59:37.350
What is that guy's nickname now?

1393
00:59:37.710 --> 00:59:38.810
Oh, my gosh.

1394
00:59:38.810 --> 00:59:39.830
What is his nickname?

1395
00:59:40.510 --> 00:59:41.670
Oh, shit is full.

1396
00:59:41.910 --> 00:59:42.550
I don't know.

1397
00:59:43.910 --> 00:59:49.990
I do have to say, this is something that I struggled with the first time I was in a trailer.

1398
00:59:50.190 --> 00:59:53.730
It took me a very long time to figure out how to flush the toilet.

1399
00:59:53.830 --> 00:59:54.170
Yes.

1400
00:59:54.350 --> 00:59:56.570
I should maybe put this in my book.

1401
00:59:56.570 --> 00:59:57.110
Next book.

1402
00:59:57.310 --> 00:59:59.070
Yeah, my acting advice book.

1403
00:59:59.470 --> 01:00:01.410
Sometimes toilets have a foot pedal.

1404
01:00:01.490 --> 01:00:02.090
Look for the foot.

1405
01:00:02.150 --> 01:00:02.790
Don't panic.

1406
01:00:03.030 --> 01:00:03.630
Don't panic.

1407
01:00:03.730 --> 01:00:06.950
Because you're already a little panicked just because you're there.

1408
01:00:07.290 --> 01:00:07.430
Yes.

1409
01:00:07.430 --> 01:00:10.650
And I, you know, you should know how to flush your toilet.

1410
01:00:10.910 --> 01:00:14.510
Well, Nick, thank you so much for sharing all of your stories with us.

1411
01:00:14.630 --> 01:00:19.490
Guys, you can follow Nick over on Instagram at ncaferronicestguy.

1412
01:00:19.670 --> 01:00:20.470
Thank you so much.

1413
01:00:20.770 --> 01:00:20.910
Yes, Nick.

1414
01:00:21.010 --> 01:00:21.870
Those were so fun.

1415
01:00:22.310 --> 01:00:24.790
Well, there's a time cut now in the conference room.

1416
01:00:24.970 --> 01:00:26.030
It's a little bit later.

1417
01:00:26.250 --> 01:00:28.050
The acapella group is still singing.

1418
01:00:28.270 --> 01:00:30.130
They're singing the song Car Wash.

1419
01:00:30.370 --> 01:00:32.150
Clark is really into it.

1420
01:00:32.490 --> 01:00:33.930
The senator nods to Oscar.

1421
01:00:34.070 --> 01:00:36.710
Looks like they're going to maybe go find a place to meet up.

1422
01:00:36.870 --> 01:00:37.250
Mm-hmm.

1423
01:00:37.950 --> 01:00:43.010
Now the acapella guys are going to say, we've got a special treat for you.

1424
01:00:43.370 --> 01:00:46.690
They start singing Andy's signature song, Faith.

1425
01:00:47.290 --> 01:00:48.570
He pops up.

1426
01:00:48.730 --> 01:00:50.070
He's shaking his tush.

1427
01:00:50.070 --> 01:00:53.110
But guess who appears on the television behind them?

1428
01:00:54.010 --> 01:00:54.890
Broccoli Robb.

1429
01:00:54.930 --> 01:00:56.550
And he's singing it, too.

1430
01:00:57.290 --> 01:00:57.710
Yeah.

1431
01:00:58.150 --> 01:00:59.710
And Andy's like, what the hell?

1432
01:00:59.810 --> 01:01:02.530
And they're like, well, this is Broccoli Robb's signature song.

1433
01:01:02.690 --> 01:01:04.050
We thought you wanted to hear it.

1434
01:01:04.190 --> 01:01:05.430
This is too much for Andy.

1435
01:01:05.730 --> 01:01:10.230
First of all, Broccoli Robb took Boner Champ from him, and now his signature song?

1436
01:01:10.410 --> 01:01:10.850
Mm-hmm.

1437
01:01:10.850 --> 01:01:13.190
We got a fan question from Sophie H.

1438
01:01:13.250 --> 01:01:15.410
in England who said, please tell us how much you had to

1439
01:01:15.410 --> 01:01:16.670
pay for all of the songs.

1440
01:01:17.030 --> 01:01:22.310
Sophie, Steve Burgess said, our music people did a lot of negotiating for these songs.

1441
01:01:22.570 --> 01:01:22.770
I bet.

1442
01:01:23.450 --> 01:01:24.830
Faith was the most expensive.

1443
01:01:25.050 --> 01:01:27.090
We paid $30,000 for Faith.

1444
01:01:27.310 --> 01:01:32.550
All of the other songs were negotiated for $20,000, and Car Wash was free.

1445
01:01:33.230 --> 01:01:33.450
Oh.

1446
01:01:33.450 --> 01:01:38.490
You know, Claire said that when she was prepping this episode, the most difficult part was

1447
01:01:38.490 --> 01:01:39.590
prepping all these songs.

1448
01:01:39.770 --> 01:01:41.990
Like you said, Angela, they did a ton of rehearsal.

1449
01:01:42.270 --> 01:01:48.510
But she said, in particular, any time people were singing and there was dialogue, it was

1450
01:01:48.510 --> 01:01:54.270
really tricky because they had to be able to get all of it, and it gets really hard

1451
01:01:54.270 --> 01:01:54.770
to cut.

1452
01:01:54.970 --> 01:01:56.290
To edit around that.

1453
01:01:56.290 --> 01:02:01.530
Yeah, Jim and I weren't always fighting or saying our lines at the exact same time as

1454
01:02:01.530 --> 01:02:02.170
other takes.

1455
01:02:02.350 --> 01:02:03.070
It's hard to do.

1456
01:02:03.210 --> 01:02:07.570
So she said, as a director, that was probably the most challenging part about shooting this

1457
01:02:07.570 --> 01:02:07.990
episode.

1458
01:02:08.190 --> 01:02:10.690
Well, we got a fan question from Cessia Z.

1459
01:02:10.910 --> 01:02:12.730
in London, Ontario, Canada.

1460
01:02:13.250 --> 01:02:18.270
Cessia says, when Here Comes Treble starts singing Faith and Broccoli Robb comes in singing,

1461
01:02:18.490 --> 01:02:22.250
he doesn't stop singing, even when Andy stops the group.

1462
01:02:22.730 --> 01:02:28.150
It made it seem like it was a recording of Broccoli Robb, but in the next scene, Andy is

1463
01:02:28.150 --> 01:02:31.010
having a whole conversation with him like it's a video chat.

1464
01:02:31.230 --> 01:02:36.330
I see the camera, but I'm wondering if there was a missing scene that explained this transition.

1465
01:02:36.750 --> 01:02:39.710
Well, there was some missing dialogue that would have explained it.

1466
01:02:40.330 --> 01:02:47.350
Per the script, Robb finally stops singing, and then he says, oh, I had the audio off on

1467
01:02:47.350 --> 01:02:50.290
my end, fellas, but it felt like I hit that one out of the park.

1468
01:02:50.570 --> 01:02:51.010
Right.

1469
01:02:51.010 --> 01:02:51.090
Right.

1470
01:02:51.990 --> 01:02:52.470
Yes.

1471
01:02:52.870 --> 01:02:54.290
But great catch, Cessia.

1472
01:02:54.570 --> 01:02:57.850
Well, like you said, Andy is going to confront Broccoli Robb now.

1473
01:02:58.270 --> 01:02:58.530
Yeah.

1474
01:02:59.290 --> 01:03:01.690
And what is up with Broccoli Robb's apartment?

1475
01:03:02.690 --> 01:03:05.350
I mean, he says he still lives close to campus.

1476
01:03:05.690 --> 01:03:07.110
Does he live in a dorm room?

1477
01:03:07.290 --> 01:03:08.350
I'm very confused.

1478
01:03:08.370 --> 01:03:10.110
What has happened to Broccoli Robb?

1479
01:03:10.370 --> 01:03:11.290
Oh, you know what?

1480
01:03:11.290 --> 01:03:13.030
I bet he's like the RA.

1481
01:03:13.610 --> 01:03:14.090
Maybe.

1482
01:03:14.270 --> 01:03:14.990
I don't know.

1483
01:03:15.110 --> 01:03:18.890
It was like he just, he looks like he's living in a frat house or something, maybe.

1484
01:03:18.890 --> 01:03:21.190
He has just like a leather couch.

1485
01:03:21.550 --> 01:03:23.810
It's not filled out in any way.

1486
01:03:23.950 --> 01:03:25.910
It looks like a lamp is sitting on the floor.

1487
01:03:26.250 --> 01:03:26.690
Yeah.

1488
01:03:26.690 --> 01:03:30.390
It's very, very college looking is what I'll say.

1489
01:03:30.750 --> 01:03:36.370
Their fight escalates to this crazy challenge where they're going to have a sing off for

1490
01:03:36.370 --> 01:03:38.310
the rights to the song, faith.

1491
01:03:38.950 --> 01:03:40.770
And Erin has had enough.

1492
01:03:40.930 --> 01:03:43.970
She just unplugs the TV because the guys are just yelling at each other.

1493
01:03:44.370 --> 01:03:47.530
Andy and Erin then have a big talk in the conference room.

1494
01:03:47.690 --> 01:03:50.990
And Erin is losing respect for Andy in all of this.

1495
01:03:50.990 --> 01:03:53.390
Like, she's like, this is kind of ridiculous, right?

1496
01:03:53.610 --> 01:03:53.910
Well, yeah.

1497
01:03:54.050 --> 01:03:58.210
She had a talking head earlier where she's like, you know, when you're with someone,

1498
01:03:58.490 --> 01:04:01.770
you just have to put up with the stuff that makes you lose respect for them.

1499
01:04:01.970 --> 01:04:02.650
That's love.

1500
01:04:02.850 --> 01:04:03.030
Yeah.

1501
01:04:03.410 --> 01:04:08.630
Andy is now going to suggest that maybe, you know, just maybe if he were closer to

1502
01:04:08.630 --> 01:04:12.390
Cornell sharing his stories, he'd be the one all the guys remember.

1503
01:04:12.450 --> 01:04:13.190
You know what?

1504
01:04:13.270 --> 01:04:13.790
Oh, my God.

1505
01:04:13.930 --> 01:04:14.990
Maybe they should move there.

1506
01:04:15.230 --> 01:04:17.010
And Erin's like, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

1507
01:04:17.010 --> 01:04:18.830
No, but then he has another idea.

1508
01:04:19.170 --> 01:04:19.950
I know.

1509
01:04:20.590 --> 01:04:26.350
What if I made a big donation from the Bernard Family Foundation?

1510
01:04:26.610 --> 01:04:27.770
To the acapella group.

1511
01:04:27.850 --> 01:04:28.150
Yes.

1512
01:04:28.270 --> 01:04:29.190
Yeah, that's it.

1513
01:04:29.330 --> 01:04:31.010
Then he would get the respect he deserves.

1514
01:04:31.250 --> 01:04:35.830
Because, and I quote, if I'm not Boner Champ, I don't know who I am.

1515
01:04:36.270 --> 01:04:36.530
Yeah.

1516
01:04:37.090 --> 01:04:39.510
Now at front reception, a group has gathered.

1517
01:04:39.510 --> 01:04:40.850
They're eating some candy.

1518
01:04:40.990 --> 01:04:42.430
They're chatting about the concert.

1519
01:04:42.830 --> 01:04:44.210
Kevin really liked it.

1520
01:04:44.210 --> 01:04:47.610
But Angela said, you know what, they lost me when they sang Monster Mash.

1521
01:04:47.990 --> 01:04:49.930
It just glorifies the occult.

1522
01:04:50.110 --> 01:04:52.250
And Jim's like, hey, you know what, Angela, relax.

1523
01:04:52.270 --> 01:04:52.930
It's Halloween.

1524
01:04:53.310 --> 01:04:54.570
It's a Halloween song.

1525
01:04:54.910 --> 01:04:55.970
They have to sing it.

1526
01:04:56.130 --> 01:04:56.670
They have to.

1527
01:04:56.890 --> 01:04:58.910
And Pam is like, oh, they have to?

1528
01:04:59.250 --> 01:05:00.790
They have to, Jim?

1529
01:05:00.990 --> 01:05:03.230
Oh, he should have never said have to.

1530
01:05:03.630 --> 01:05:04.430
That was it.

1531
01:05:04.830 --> 01:05:05.550
That's right.

1532
01:05:05.750 --> 01:05:07.930
What would happen if they didn't sing it, Jim?

1533
01:05:08.050 --> 01:05:09.110
Would someone go to jail?

1534
01:05:09.310 --> 01:05:10.290
Would they be shot?

1535
01:05:10.290 --> 01:05:16.290
That I'm generally interested in knowing your definition of have to is basically what she's

1536
01:05:16.290 --> 01:05:16.510
saying.

1537
01:05:17.130 --> 01:05:21.750
One of the funniest things during the scene to me is Brian as Kevin, his performance.

1538
01:05:21.750 --> 01:05:22.850
He looks at you.

1539
01:05:23.010 --> 01:05:26.890
He's trying to sort out Pam's rationale in this argument.

1540
01:05:27.030 --> 01:05:29.330
And then he looks at Jim and he's just going, huh?

1541
01:05:29.650 --> 01:05:35.670
I'll have you know that as producer, I would get scripts very early.

1542
01:05:35.670 --> 01:05:41.270
And when I read this Monster Mash scene, I was unsure about it.

1543
01:05:41.470 --> 01:05:49.970
I turned in my notes and I said, I really felt like Jim and Pam should have like a spy

1544
01:05:49.970 --> 01:05:53.350
shot real fight about this.

1545
01:05:53.550 --> 01:05:55.830
I didn't think it should be played comedically.

1546
01:05:56.550 --> 01:05:57.570
This was my note.

1547
01:05:57.770 --> 01:06:00.110
I'm going to say I stand corrected.

1548
01:06:00.110 --> 01:06:01.610
I really like this scene.

1549
01:06:01.790 --> 01:06:03.030
I love how it came out.

1550
01:06:03.030 --> 01:06:09.010
But I had sent back in my notes a whole pitch for what I thought the dialogue should have

1551
01:06:09.010 --> 01:06:12.710
been between Jim and Pam in terms of this argument.

1552
01:06:13.150 --> 01:06:17.950
I clearly was writing for a drama, but here's how I thought it should have played out.

1553
01:06:18.650 --> 01:06:22.530
I wanted them to find us in the middle of a fight in a spy shot.

1554
01:06:22.690 --> 01:06:24.250
And here's how it would have gone.

1555
01:06:24.610 --> 01:06:27.850
Jim would say, you have to let me make judgment calls.

1556
01:06:27.990 --> 01:06:28.910
This is a new business.

1557
01:06:29.090 --> 01:06:30.110
You weren't in the room.

1558
01:06:30.110 --> 01:06:33.710
I really felt like in order to be taken seriously, I had to inveSt.

1559
01:06:33.990 --> 01:06:35.830
You can't micromanage this, Pam.

1560
01:06:36.210 --> 01:06:41.510
And then Pam would have said, I'm not telling you what office to get or what clients to take,

1561
01:06:41.610 --> 01:06:45.270
but I must get a say in what happens with our money.

1562
01:06:45.290 --> 01:06:48.150
If it's about our family, I have a say.

1563
01:06:48.470 --> 01:06:50.930
And Jim said, exactly.

1564
01:06:50.930 --> 01:06:53.030
And you agreed we could inveSt.

1565
01:06:53.710 --> 01:06:57.750
And Pam would have said, that's when I thought we had to inveSt.

1566
01:06:58.230 --> 01:07:02.710
And Jim said, you're acting like I'm doing this for something other than our family.

1567
01:07:02.870 --> 01:07:03.950
That's the whole point.

1568
01:07:04.150 --> 01:07:05.790
And Pam would have said, really?

1569
01:07:05.990 --> 01:07:08.930
Because part of me feels like you're just doing it for you.

1570
01:07:09.590 --> 01:07:11.090
Well, that's a real fight.

1571
01:07:11.270 --> 01:07:11.730
I know.

1572
01:07:11.730 --> 01:07:18.270
So that's like taken out of almost every marriage fight out there, versions of that.

1573
01:07:18.470 --> 01:07:23.850
And I put in parentheses in my notes, maybe that last part is too far and better saved

1574
01:07:23.850 --> 01:07:25.070
for later in the season.

1575
01:07:25.310 --> 01:07:26.990
But I still want it to happen.

1576
01:07:27.770 --> 01:07:32.950
But, you know, what I was going for was I wanted to get into the nitty gritty of this

1577
01:07:32.950 --> 01:07:33.430
situation.

1578
01:07:33.470 --> 01:07:36.930
I wanted Jim to stand up for himself a little bit.

1579
01:07:36.930 --> 01:07:42.830
Because in the way that this is happening, I can tell you right now, I could never be

1580
01:07:42.830 --> 01:07:43.530
married to Jim.

1581
01:07:43.910 --> 01:07:49.570
The hemming and the hawing, the wishy-washy, and then the big swings into impulsive behavior,

1582
01:07:49.850 --> 01:07:52.250
this would drive me absolutely nuts.

1583
01:07:52.590 --> 01:07:54.410
Like, I couldn't handle it.

1584
01:07:54.490 --> 01:07:59.610
And so I think that, you know, I wanted to handle it how Jenna would handle it.

1585
01:07:59.730 --> 01:08:00.010
Right.

1586
01:08:00.150 --> 01:08:00.950
Not how Pam.

1587
01:08:01.210 --> 01:08:06.290
Luckily, there was a room full of writers who made sure that Pam handled it how Pam would

1588
01:08:06.290 --> 01:08:06.790
handle it.

1589
01:08:08.930 --> 01:08:15.610
Well, Claire shared with us that this scene leads to one of her favorite Kevin Talking

1590
01:08:15.610 --> 01:08:16.050
Heads.

1591
01:08:16.170 --> 01:08:17.710
It's also one of my favorites.

1592
01:08:18.010 --> 01:08:19.270
Also one of my favorites.

1593
01:08:19.390 --> 01:08:20.570
And I thought we should hear it.

1594
01:08:20.850 --> 01:08:26.910
It turns out Pam really, really hates Monster Mash.

1595
01:08:27.150 --> 01:08:31.310
I mean, like, never bring that song up in front of her.

1596
01:08:31.310 --> 01:08:40.790
Even though Jim was making great points, like in favor of the song, Pam was like, no, hate

1597
01:08:40.790 --> 01:08:42.150
it, stupid.

1598
01:08:45.720 --> 01:08:50.500
You know, this is the moment where a lot of people turn on Pam, too, because they think she's

1599
01:08:50.500 --> 01:08:54.800
being irrationally angry at Jim because he did something that she agreed to.

1600
01:08:54.800 --> 01:08:55.320
Yeah.

1601
01:08:55.320 --> 01:09:00.540
But you're missing when we originally wrote this episode, he did do something without asking

1602
01:09:00.540 --> 01:09:03.140
her, which was investing more than they agreed on.

1603
01:09:03.420 --> 01:09:03.600
Yeah.

1604
01:09:03.720 --> 01:09:05.080
When he didn't have to at all.

1605
01:09:05.120 --> 01:09:06.240
When he didn't have to at all.

1606
01:09:06.240 --> 01:09:12.780
I want you to know in the original script, there was a beat that I did successfully argue should

1607
01:09:12.780 --> 01:09:14.600
be cut, and I stand by it.

1608
01:09:15.080 --> 01:09:20.420
When Jim and Pam are leaving for the day and they get in their car, Jim turns on Monster

1609
01:09:20.420 --> 01:09:26.500
Mash and looks at Pam as a way of trying to smooth things over.

1610
01:09:26.500 --> 01:09:27.660
Oh, my gosh.

1611
01:09:27.940 --> 01:09:28.620
And I was like.

1612
01:09:28.740 --> 01:09:29.960
That's kind of a dick move.

1613
01:09:30.260 --> 01:09:34.200
I was like, I don't think Pam's going to have a real sense of humor for that.

1614
01:09:34.560 --> 01:09:34.760
Yeah.

1615
01:09:34.980 --> 01:09:35.720
You know what?

1616
01:09:35.840 --> 01:09:37.400
Kevin could tell you not to do that.

1617
01:09:37.680 --> 01:09:42.880
It was pitched maybe it would make Pam laugh, and I said, I think we need to leave the tension.

1618
01:09:43.460 --> 01:09:43.680
Yeah.

1619
01:09:44.020 --> 01:09:45.820
No, she wouldn't move on that quickly.

1620
01:09:46.100 --> 01:09:47.040
I didn't think so.

1621
01:09:47.540 --> 01:09:50.920
Well, back to this Dwight Nellie mom detective moment.

1622
01:09:51.080 --> 01:09:53.700
Nellie eventually says, Dwight, look, it's my pill, all right?

1623
01:09:53.800 --> 01:09:54.720
I deal with some anxiety.

1624
01:09:54.720 --> 01:09:55.700
It's not a big deal.

1625
01:09:55.700 --> 01:09:59.440
And I think this kind of puts life in perspective for Dwight.

1626
01:09:59.680 --> 01:10:00.920
He says, you know what?

1627
01:10:01.260 --> 01:10:06.440
I might want some of those pills for my cousin because he's had a tough time being wifeless

1628
01:10:06.440 --> 01:10:10.220
with a high-pressure job, and also he has a crazy cousin named Moe's.

1629
01:10:10.600 --> 01:10:11.820
And Nellie says, you know what?

1630
01:10:11.860 --> 01:10:13.980
He's a good man, and she hopes he feels better.

1631
01:10:14.740 --> 01:10:17.220
Yes, he's clearly talking about himself.

1632
01:10:17.660 --> 01:10:23.360
And we got a fan question from Jade O in Los Angeles who said, Dwight talks to Nellie

1633
01:10:23.360 --> 01:10:25.900
about getting a prescription for anxiety medicine.

1634
01:10:26.420 --> 01:10:30.960
And then later, he reveals in the Christmas episode that he has been taking them.

1635
01:10:31.480 --> 01:10:35.460
Is this the reason why he seems so much calmer in the rest of the series?

1636
01:10:35.780 --> 01:10:40.380
It felt like there was a shift in his personality, and he went through a lot of character growth.

1637
01:10:40.640 --> 01:10:45.560
He seemed much happier and friendlier to everyone for the rest of the series after this episode.

1638
01:10:45.900 --> 01:10:48.320
Jade, I am going to track that now.

1639
01:10:48.320 --> 01:10:50.280
Yeah, I'm going to pay attention.

1640
01:10:50.580 --> 01:10:52.060
This is a great observation.

1641
01:10:52.420 --> 01:10:56.460
I mean, I know they were setting up Dwight for a possible spinoff in the farm,

1642
01:10:57.300 --> 01:11:01.780
and they needed him to be able to leave Dunder Mifflin.

1643
01:11:01.900 --> 01:11:07.420
So they were setting up Dwight to sort of have some big life realization moments.

1644
01:11:07.800 --> 01:11:09.520
His job there is stressful.

1645
01:11:09.940 --> 01:11:11.200
He is wifeless.

1646
01:11:11.360 --> 01:11:14.340
Like, these things that might make him move on to another place.

1647
01:11:14.980 --> 01:11:21.460
This episode wraps up with a bit of a montage, during which several things happen.

1648
01:11:21.820 --> 01:11:24.500
We find out that Andy's parents are broke.

1649
01:11:24.760 --> 01:11:24.960
Yeah.

1650
01:11:25.620 --> 01:11:29.960
Toby tries to bring some flowers to Nellie, but when she takes her Toby wig off,

1651
01:11:30.060 --> 01:11:31.340
he's no longer interested.

1652
01:11:31.660 --> 01:11:33.980
I looked what it said in the shooting draft for that.

1653
01:11:34.120 --> 01:11:34.940
What did it say?

1654
01:11:35.200 --> 01:11:37.560
Says Nellie is packing up to leave for the day.

1655
01:11:37.900 --> 01:11:40.780
Toby appears from the annex, approaches her holding some flowers.

1656
01:11:40.960 --> 01:11:41.780
He looks nervous.

1657
01:11:41.780 --> 01:11:47.480
Nellie, not noticing him, pulls off her Toby wig, releasing her normal hair.

1658
01:11:47.960 --> 01:11:50.500
Something in Toby dies.

1659
01:11:51.100 --> 01:11:52.420
Nellie notices him.

1660
01:11:52.600 --> 01:11:53.040
Hi, Toby.

1661
01:11:53.160 --> 01:11:54.060
Who are the flowers for?

1662
01:11:54.300 --> 01:11:54.920
Toby.

1663
01:11:55.440 --> 01:11:56.060
Nobody.

1664
01:11:56.620 --> 01:11:59.460
He throws the flowers in a trash can and crosses off.

1665
01:12:00.080 --> 01:12:00.260
Hmm.

1666
01:12:00.940 --> 01:12:02.200
It's over for him.

1667
01:12:02.580 --> 01:12:04.700
Toby just wanted Toby.

1668
01:12:05.460 --> 01:12:13.040
And finally, we have a spy shot of the senator and Oscar outside, and they are making out.

1669
01:12:13.180 --> 01:12:14.600
They are making out.

1670
01:12:14.760 --> 01:12:18.540
And then as they part ways, Oscar sees the camera.

1671
01:12:18.700 --> 01:12:19.180
Yeah.

1672
01:12:19.360 --> 01:12:19.780
Busted.

1673
01:12:20.480 --> 01:12:23.120
Well, everyone, that was Here Comes Treble.

1674
01:12:23.120 --> 01:12:29.260
Well, a big thank you to Halstead Sullivan, Claire Scanlon, Nick Caferro, Steve Burgess.

1675
01:12:29.500 --> 01:12:30.640
What an episode.

1676
01:12:31.020 --> 01:12:33.680
And thanks, you guys, for sending in your questions and comments.

1677
01:12:33.680 --> 01:12:35.040
We love hearing from you.

1678
01:12:35.240 --> 01:12:36.220
See you next week.

1679
01:12:41.740 --> 01:12:43.580
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.

1680
01:12:43.920 --> 01:12:48.000
Office Ladies is produced by Earwolf, Jenna Fisher, and Angela Kinsey.

1681
01:12:48.000 --> 01:12:50.380
Our senior producer is Cassie Jerkins.

1682
01:12:50.560 --> 01:12:52.660
Our in-studio engineer is Sam Kiefer.

1683
01:12:52.820 --> 01:12:55.060
Our editing and mixing engineer is Jordan Duffy.

1684
01:12:55.220 --> 01:12:57.440
And our associate producer is Ainsley Bubbico.

1685
01:12:57.680 --> 01:13:00.540
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
